---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Source Policy"
  description="The primary-source hierarchy, excluded sources, citation requirements, and review statuses used by Komadrona Review."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Evidence and content governance</span>
      <h1>Source policy</h1>
      <p>Content must be traceable, current enough for its purpose, and written without copying protected question banks.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <article class="container prose">
    <h2>Source hierarchy</h2>
    <p>Komadrona Review prioritizes sources in this order:</p>

    <ol>
      <li>Current PRC and Professional Regulatory Board of Midwifery examination programs and resolutions</li>
      <li>Philippine statutes and official issuances relevant to midwifery practice</li>
      <li>Current Department of Health manuals, administrative orders, circulars, and national programs</li>
      <li>Current CHED midwifery education standards and competencies</li>
      <li>Current WHO recommendations and other recognized international primary guidance</li>
      <li>Peer-reviewed literature and properly licensed educational references used only as supporting material</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Initial official references</h2>
    <ul class="source-list">
      <li>
        <strong>PRC — Revised April 2026 Midwives Licensure Examination Program</strong>
        <span>Used to identify the five examination subject headings and integrated supporting disciplines.</span>
        <a href="https://www.prc.gov.ph/sites/default/files/Revised%20Exam%20Program%20for%20Midwives.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open official PDF</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Republic Act No. 7392 — Philippine Midwifery Act of 1992</strong>
        <span>Used for statutory scope, professional regulation, and examination-subject context.</span>
        <a href="https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1992/ra_7392_1992.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Lawphil copy</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>National Privacy Commission — Data Privacy Act and Implementing Rules</strong>
        <span>Used for transparency, legitimate purpose, proportionality, security, and retention principles.</span>
        <a href="https://privacy.gov.ph/implementing-rules-regulations-data-privacy-act-2012/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open NPC publication</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Department of Health</strong>
        <span>Primary Philippine source for current maternal, newborn, public-health, and clinical program guidance.</span>
        <a href="https://doh.gov.ph/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open DOH website</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Commission on Higher Education</strong>
        <span>Primary source for current Philippine midwifery education policies, standards, and competencies.</span>
        <a href="https://ched.gov.ph/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open CHED website</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>World Health Organization</strong>
        <span>International guidance used where applicable and reconciled with current Philippine policy.</span>
        <a href="https://www.who.int/health-topics/maternal-health" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open WHO maternal health topic</a>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Required metadata</h2>
    <p>Every published review topic should identify:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the examination domain and topic;</li>
      <li>the exact source title, issuing body, publication date or version, and relevant section;</li>
      <li>the date the source was checked;</li>
      <li>the article's content status; and</li>
      <li>corrections or superseded guidance where relevant.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Content statuses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Draft:</strong> not available as relied-upon review material.</li>
      <li><strong>Source checked:</strong> citations and core statements were compared with identified sources.</li>
      <li><strong>Clinically reviewed:</strong> reviewed by a qualified professional whose role and consent are recorded.</li>
      <li><strong>Needs re-verification:</strong> a source may have changed or the review interval has expired.</li>
      <li><strong>Archived:</strong> retained for correction history but removed from current study paths.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sources not accepted as authority</h2>
    <p>The following may help locate a topic but cannot serve as the final source of record:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>unsourced social-media posts, short-form videos, anonymous blogs, and AI-generated text;</li>
      <li>Quizlet, CourseHero, Scribd uploads, and similar user-upload repositories;</li>
      <li>commercial reviewer scans, copied textbook pages, and proprietary test banks;</li>
      <li>recalled, reconstructed, leaked, or claimed actual board-examination questions; and</li>
      <li>outdated guidance when a current official replacement exists.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Writing and copyright rule</h2>
    <p>
      Explanations and practice questions must be written originally. Public access to a document does not by itself
      authorize copying an entire table, illustration, chapter, or question bank. Short quotations must be necessary,
      attributed, and limited. External documents should normally be linked rather than rehosted.
    </p>

    <p class="small-print">Policy version: 1.0 — 3 August 2026.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
